'''''An Unknown Enemy''''' ({{langx|es|Un Extraño Enemigo}}) is a 2018 television [[History|historical]] [[political thriller]]<ref>{{Cite web | url=https://diariojudio.com/noticias/un-extrano-enemigo-de-gabriel-ripstein-se-estrenara-en-amazon-prime-video/276345/ | title="Un Extraño Enemigo" de Gabriel Ripstein se estrenará en Amazon Prime Video |website=Diariojudio.com| date=2018-08-10}}</ref> and drama series released on [[Amazon Prime]].

It examines the events leading to the [[Tlatelolco massacre|1968 student massacre]] and its cover-up, through the eyes of Commander Fernando Barrientos, head of a secret [[Intelligence agency]].<ref>{{Cite web | url=https://www.forbes.com.mx/forbes-life/5-peliculas-y-series-para-no-olvidar-el-2-de-octubre/ | title=5 películas y series para no olvidar el 2 de octubre |website=Forbes.com.mx}}</ref>

The series main character is loosely based on the real life [[Fernando Gutiérrez Barrios]], director of the infamous [[Dirección Federal de Seguridad|DFS]] intelligence Agency, and depicts the political intrigues that triggered [[Dirty War (Mexico)|the period of censorship and repression of students at the end of the 1960s]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://elfinanciero.com.mx/culturas/amazon-estrena-un-extrano-enemigo-una-trama-sobre-el-68-vista-desde-el-poder|title=Amazon estrena 'Un extraño enemigo', una trama sobre el 68 vista desde el poder|website=El Financiero}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://lifeandstyle.mx/entretenimiento/2018/06/01/un-extrano-enemigo-la-serie-inspirada-en-la-masacre-de-tlatelolco-del-68|title='Un Extraño Enemigo', la serie inspirada en la masacre de Tlatelolco del 68|date=1 June 2018|website=Life and Style}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://suracapulco.mx/2018/09/27/retratan-en-serie-las-maniobras-politicas-que-llevaron-a-la-masacre-de-tlatelolco/|title=Retratan en serie las maniobras políticas que llevaron a la masacre de Tlatelolco|date=27 September 2018|website=El Sur de Acapulco I Periódico de Guerrero}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://news.culturacolectiva.com/mexico/un-extrano-enemigo-la-serie-de-amazon-que-habla-de-los-politicos-en-el-68/|title=¿Quieres saber qué pensaban Díaz Ordaz y Luis Echeverría en el 68?|date=27 September 2018|website=News.culturacolectiva.com}}</ref>

Season 1, comprising eight episodes, aired on Amazon Prime exclusively. It premiered on October 2, 2018, commemorating 50 years of the depicted events.<ref>{{Cite web | url=http://www.elfinanciero.com.mx/culturas/amazon-estrena-un-extrano-enemigo-una-trama-sobre-el-68-vista-desde-el-poder | title=Amazon estrena 'Un extraño enemigo', una trama sobre el 68 vista desde el poder|website=Elfinanciero.com.mx}}</ref> On November 9, 2018, it was announced that the series would be renewed for a second season which premiered on September 28, 2022. This season its losely based on Corpus Christi Massacre and subsequently guerrilla groups 3 years after the events of the first season.<ref>{{Cite web | url=https://www.eluniversal.com.mx/espectaculos/un-extrano-enemigo-tendra-segunda-temporada | title="Un extraño enemigo" tendrá segunda temporada|website=Eluniversal.com.mx| date=2018-11-15}}</ref>

==Premise==

=== Season 1 ===
''An Unknown Enemy'' explores the origins of the Mexican [[Mexican Dirty War|dirty war]] of the 1960s, and portrays the attempts of Fernando Barrientos, head of the "NSD" secret police, to ensure a grip on political power, as the country goes through a series of social turmoils, in part provoked by the agency he is directing. All happening in the frame of the [[Cold War]], the [[Counterculture of the 1960s|1960s youth counterculture]], the preparations of [[1968 Summer Olympics|1968 Olympic Games]] in Mexico and the upcoming [[1970 Mexican general election]]. 

=== Season 2 ===
The second season covers the aftermath of movement, el halconazo, the guerrilla groups and barrientos return on the power.
